The  command  displays  or sets the parameters that determine the
playback and recording format for software using an audio device.
It is most useful when the full API is not available,  e.g.  when
playing  or  recording  raw audio data from a script, or from the
command line.  It does not control the underlying  hardware  for‐
mat,  which  can  be  changed  with The variables that can be in‐
spected and changed with are normally per‐application and are re‐
set when a device is opened.  This can be circumvented  by  using
instead,  which  retains global state.  If a list of variables is
present on the command line, then prints  the  current  value  of
those  variables for the specified device.  If the flag is speci‐
fied, all variables for the device are printed.  If the  flag  is
specified  attempts  to  set the specified variables to the given
values.  The flag can be used to give an alternative  audio  con‐
